#: ../../source/docs/finding-the-particular-commit-which-introduced-a-bug.rst:5
#: 68031e3d0a3e426395007f9cdb191427
msgid "Finding the Particular Commit which Introduced a Bug"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/finding-the-particular-commit-which-introduced-a-bug.rst:7
#: 57063f42e7894bab8cc362585dc9a02d
msgid "This article explains how to perform a firmware binary `bisection search <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bisection_method>`__. This is an efficient technique to find the particular build/commit that introduced a reproducible bug."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/finding-the-particular-commit-which-introduced-a-bug.rst:13
#: 1b8d7b28c4924affa10be1f772368f1c
msgid "Knowing the build in which a defect was first introduced can help identify possible causes of the problem, and inform analysis of logs and other debug techniques."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/finding-the-particular-commit-which-introduced-a-bug.rst:17
#: 612f77e7898c4f0abc99d733f780aa43
msgid "Firmware builds are available from `firmware.ardupilot.org <https://firmware.ardupilot.org/>`__ for each vehicle-type: \\ `Copter <https://firmware.ardupilot.org/Copter/>`__, `Plane <https://firmware.ardupilot.org/Plane/>`__, `Rover <https://firmware.ardupilot.org/Rover>`__, `AntennaTracker <https://firmware.ardupilot.org/AntennaTracker/>`__. To perform a bisection search:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/finding-the-particular-commit-which-introduced-a-bug.rst:25
#: b1ff8d13b39a4640bed66fade13a6151
msgid "First test the firmware build half-way between the known working and failing builds. The result gives you a new \"known working\" or \"known failing\" build and halves the number of builds that must be tested."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/finding-the-particular-commit-which-introduced-a-bug.rst:28
#: 7482e3019efb49cba6e57920993b8376
msgid "Repeat this test process, each time halving the size of the test range, until the problem build has been identified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/finding-the-particular-commit-which-introduced-a-bug.rst:31
#: c9c4af34a9034f57a6d058601d2e0057
msgid "Once you have identified the problem issue, note the build number and include this in your bug report."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/finding-the-particular-commit-which-introduced-a-bug.rst:36
#: 9b0af00bf78e496eab06c9d71755efe9
msgid "The autotest system generates a new firmware build for every commit to the source tree (this is a slight simplification, as commits may be batched if they arrive while a previous build is being tested). This means that if an error is reproducible it is possible to identify the specific commit(s) in which it first occurs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/finding-the-particular-commit-which-introduced-a-bug.rst:41
#: 85e94519bbf64a65b1b5921710866418
msgid "Given the number of ArduPilot firmware builds it should be possible to locate the problem build/commit within around 10 tests (at time of writing)."
msgstr ""
